        <p>For Coughs and. Colds.</p>
        <p>"T BE MISLED-</p>
        <p>Death of Dr. W. H. Hughes The death took place on Sunday of Dr. William Henry Hughes, of Harwood, Mossley-road, Ashton- under-Lyne, after a long illness. Dr. Hughes, who amongst other appointments had held that of medical officer of health for the borough was educated at the Winwick and Warrington Grammar Schools, and afterwards entered the Royal School of Medicine, Manchester, and the Royal Infirmary as a student. He subsequently went to the London Untversity Medical College and graduated as M.R.C.S. and L S.D. He received the appointment of resident surgeon at the Manchester Infirmary and was afterwards the resident medical officer of the Chorlton Union Hospital, Man- chester. He was the author of several medical works, including "The Responsibtlities of Sanitary Authori- ties " and "The Operations of the Public Health Act. '</p>
