        <p>Wants New Clothes. James Cullen, a stranger, who appeared in the dock at the Warrington Borough Court on Thursday i morning, clothed only n a rug, was charged with having been drunk and disorderly in Iforsemarket- street on Wednesday night. Police-constable Tolley proved the case, and it was stated that the prisoner had torn up all his clothes during the night. The ' magistrates committed him to gaol for one month with hard labour.</p>
