      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-02-17_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <head>Market Theft.</head>
        <p>Market Theft.</p>
        <p>A young woman named Mary ConnelL'of Widnes, visited the Warrington market on Wednesday after- noon, and when at the stall of Thomas Edward Lee, a draper, she took a silk blouse and placed it in a bag which she was carrying. Mrs. Lee, however, detected her, and Connell was given into custody. At the Borough Court on Thursday she appeared very penitent, and said she was suddenly tempted.—The magistrates decided to take a lenient view of the case, and after recording a conviction she was allowed tO go</p>
      </div>
