      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-02-17_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <head>Warrington Win at Millom.</head>
        <p>Warrington Win at Millom.</p>
        <p>The return match with Mißorn was played on Satur- day at Millon and again resulted in a victory for War- rington. Both sides were strongly represented, hut the wind and heavy ground prevented accurate football. Teams : Millom—P. Harris, hack; F'. Austin, E. Jackson, A.H. Sirett, and Gilbert, three-quarter backs ; W. Barnes and S. Wallace, half backs ; J. L. ciampitt. S Richards, J. Holmes, W. Mellon, J. Troughton, J. Richardson, J. Richardson (2), and W. Dixon, forwards. Warrington—Berry, back ; Brooks, Taylor, Jones, and Harris, three-quarter backs ; Lee and Hockenhall, half hacks ; Preston, Boardman, Swift, Thomas, Harmer, Jolley, Shugars, and Heath, forwards. Referee, Nfr.D. Noble, Barrow; touch judges, Messrs. R. Casson, Ulverston, and W. H. Hall, Holme. Preston kicked off for Warrington against a cross wind, and for the first few minutes play was danger- ously near the Millom line, Wallace and Barnes eventu- ally getting the ball away to the centre by judicious touch kicking. A penalty against Millom,however,gave Warrington a footing in the home quarter, and Brookes and Harris were each within a few yards of the line. A fine tackle by Austin caused a scrummage on the home quarter line, from which Jackson and Gilbert rushed play to the other eat!, where the Warrington forwards were penalised for faulty packing, and Austin just missed the goal. Just before half-time Millom attacked strongly, and Jackson was almost over. A slight injury to P. Harris caused him to leave the field, rid the interval came with no score. In the second portion Warrington were early in evi- dence, and eventually a strong rush by the forwards left Preston in possession over the line. The same player made no mistake with the place kick. Millom through Austin and Gilbert, attacked strongly after this, and Austin was unfortunate in failing to get through after passing everybody but Shugars. From the ensuim.t scrummage the Warrington forwards raced down the field, and Harmer scored. The place kick by Hockenhall was successful. Result :—Warrington 2 goals, 2 tries (10 points). Millom nil.</p>
      </div>
