        <p>! other that had over been convened, there was a large company of earnest religious wen ; even of praying Imen. lhere were great and imperious imperial [ questions that demanded the most religious settle ment. Many wrongs needed to be set right- ' and many -rirdit things which had hitherto no been attempted needed to be promptly taken in hand and done. The men who had been sent to the House of Commons to accomplish these things by the advocacy; land votes of multitudes of Free Churchmen needed to be upheld by the prayers of Free Churchmen and women and they must all of them, contlibute their share of constant intercession on their behalf. After a reference to Dr. Horton's (President of the National Council of the Evangelical Free Churches) call to universal prayer, and to the supremely difficult question of religious teaching in the schools and colleges supported out of the rates and taxes of the nation " ; the Rev. John Yonge put it before the congregation not only RS a Christian but as a patriotic duty to pray for the new Parliament, the Cabinet, the great majority which- had entrusted to it such tremendous power, for the Opposi- tion which, " having sown the wind is reaping the whirlwind," and was so sadly a house divided against Itself," and also to pray that the men of politics might realize that upright principle was the true soul of politics; that party was to be ever subordinated to the responsibilities of State and to pray that "all things may be so ordered and settled that peace and happiness, truth and justice, religion and piety, may, be established among us for all generations." PROPOSED MOTOR 'BUS SERVICE FOR LEIGH. ' The South Lancashire Tram*eys Company are con- ducting motor 'bus trials at Leigh, with a view to establishing a service to feed their main lines of tram- ways which run from Liverpool to Bolton, Leigh, and —with the exception of a short length—to Manchester. The Leigh Corporation Tramways and Electrioity Committee are also considering the respective merits of the motor 'bus or branch tramways system within the borough.</p>
